WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Day 1, 6:42 PM.

00:04.000 --> 00:06.000
The bunker door seals behind you.

00:06.000 --> 00:08.600
This video is made by ChannelRecipe Studio

00:08.600 --> 00:10.800
on a brand new Windows computer.

00:10.800 --> 00:13.200
In this full course, we'll go from a fresh account

00:13.200 --> 00:16.000
to this exact video, step-by-step.

00:16.000 --> 00:20.000
Every click, every setting, in order.

00:20.000 --> 00:21.300
You need three things.

00:21.300 --> 00:24.300
ChannelRecipe Studio, the Claude desktop app,

00:24.300 --> 00:27.700
and a Kie.ai account for the voice and pictures.

00:27.700 --> 00:29.300
We'll set up all three together.

00:31.300 --> 00:33.700
Once you've subscribed, you'll see this.

00:33.700 --> 00:35.700
Click Setup Studio.

00:35.700 --> 00:38.700
That opens the setup page with three steps.

00:38.700 --> 00:41.700
Download Studio, install, and connect it.

00:41.700 --> 00:43.700
Then make your first video.

00:43.700 --> 00:45.700
Under step 1, pick Windows

00:45.700 --> 00:48.700
and click Download ChannelRecipe Studio.

00:48.700 --> 00:51.700
It's a zip file, about 250 megabytes.

00:51.700 --> 00:54.700
There's also a short setup video on this page

00:54.700 --> 00:56.700
if you want the quick version.

00:57.700 --> 01:02.100
While that downloads, install the Claude desktop app.

01:02.100 --> 01:04.300
Search for Claude desktop app.

01:04.300 --> 01:08.700
Open the official download page and click Download for Windows.

01:08.700 --> 01:12.700
The installer runs by itself. Give it a few minutes.

01:16.700 --> 01:21.700
When Claude opens, accept the cookie settings. Click Get Started and sign in with your email.

01:21.700 --> 01:26.700
Claude sends you a sign-in link. Open it and when your browser asks, choose Open Link.

01:26.700 --> 01:27.700
Choose Open Link.

01:28.700 --> 01:29.700
You're signed in.

01:30.700 --> 01:33.700
If Claude asks for access to your camera, you can say no.

01:33.700 --> 01:34.700
You won't need it.

01:36.700 --> 01:38.700
Now unzip Studio.

01:38.700 --> 01:40.700
Open your Downloads folder.

01:40.700 --> 01:42.700
Right-click the ChannelRecipe zip.

01:42.700 --> 01:43.700
Choose Extract All.

01:43.700 --> 01:45.700
And click Extract.

01:46.700 --> 01:49.700
Back in Claude, open the Code tab.

01:49.700 --> 01:52.700
Under the Message box, click the folder picker.

01:52.700 --> 01:59.200
Choose Open Folder and select the ChannelRecipe Studio folder inside the one you just extracted.

01:59.200 --> 02:02.200
Then, click Trust Workspace.

02:02.200 --> 02:05.200
Set the permissions to bypass permissions.

02:05.200 --> 02:10.700
So, Claude Code can install things without stopping to ask you every few seconds and confirm.

02:10.700 --> 02:13.200
Leave the model on Sonnet.

02:15.200 --> 02:17.200
Go back to the setup page.

02:17.200 --> 02:19.700
Under Step 2, copy the install prompt.

02:19.700 --> 02:22.200
Paste it into Claude Code and press Enter.

02:22.200 --> 02:28.080
Claude Code reads the folder, checks what your computer already has, like Python and Node,

02:28.080 --> 02:36.460
and starts the Studio Installer.

02:36.460 --> 02:41.540
Windows asks if you want to run the installer, untick

02:41.540 --> 02:46.020
Always ask before opening this file, and click Run.

02:46.020 --> 02:49.300
Now the installer downloads everything Studio needs.

02:49.300 --> 02:57.060
When it's done, Studio opens its setup page in your browser, all by itself.

02:57.060 --> 02:58.940
First, the tools check.

02:58.940 --> 03:02.100
Python, the graphics browser, and the network are ready.

03:02.100 --> 03:06.940
The video tools and the YouTube helper aren't installed yet, so click Fix it on each one,

03:06.940 --> 03:09.780
and Studio downloads them for you.

03:09.780 --> 03:12.900
Wait until every line says ready.

03:12.900 --> 03:13.900
Step 1.

03:13.900 --> 03:15.980
Connect your ChannelRecipe account.

03:15.980 --> 03:18.460
Click the button, then approve and connect.

03:18.460 --> 03:25.940
You're sent straight back and step one says done. Step two, set up Claude, click install

03:25.940 --> 03:31.780
Claude Code. Studio runs Anthropic's official installer for you. Click open the

03:31.780 --> 03:36.620
sign-in window, sign in with your Claude account, open the link from your email

03:36.620 --> 03:43.900
and click Authorize. Back in Studio, click Setup Claude for videos. It connects,

03:43.900 --> 03:49.900
picks the Claude models and runs a quick check with each one.

03:49.900 --> 03:50.900
Step 3.

03:50.900 --> 03:53.660
Voice and Images.

03:53.660 --> 03:58.900
By default, Studio narrates with Gemini Voices through Kie.ai, and if you have your own

03:58.900 --> 04:01.900
ElevenLabs account, you can pick that instead.

04:01.900 --> 04:07.900
Copy your API key from your Kie dashboard, paste it in, and click Check and Connect Media

04:07.900 --> 04:08.900
account.

04:08.900 --> 04:11.900
Kie is connected, and Step 3 is done.

04:11.900 --> 04:14.400
That's set up done. Click Open Studio.

04:19.500 --> 04:22.200
If there's an update banner at the top, take it.

04:22.200 --> 04:25.400
Click Update Now, then Restart Now.

04:25.400 --> 04:27.400
The page reloads on the new version

04:27.400 --> 04:29.400
and your projects, accounts, and styles

04:29.400 --> 04:31.400
stay exactly as they were.

04:33.900 --> 04:37.400
Now the fun part, Cloning a Channel's Style.

04:37.400 --> 04:40.900
Go to Style Library and click Clone a Style.

04:40.900 --> 04:43.580
You need a channel to learn from.

04:43.580 --> 04:46.780
We searched YouTube for zombie apocalypse day one,

04:46.780 --> 04:49.820
opened one of these stick figure survival videos,

04:49.820 --> 04:52.620
and went to the channel, Nobody Gets In,

04:52.620 --> 04:54.060
copy the channel's link.

04:56.100 --> 04:58.540
Paste it into YouTube reference link,

04:58.540 --> 05:01.260
and click Preview References.

05:01.260 --> 05:04.100
Studio lists the channel's videos.

05:04.100 --> 05:06.460
Tick up to three that show the style best,

05:06.460 --> 05:08.980
and click Look at these videos.

05:08.980 --> 05:18.980
Studio now reads each video's captions, downloads the first three minutes, and measures the pacing, the motion, the light, and the sound.

05:18.980 --> 05:26.980
It takes a few minutes, and the download can look slow. That's normal. Let it run. Then you get.

05:26.980 --> 05:35.980
Here's what Studio saw. It recommends a recipe here, 2D life stories, and lists what makes the channel recognizable.

05:35.980 --> 05:42.980
Rigged stick figure characters, a new picture about every two seconds, hard cuts, a vignette,

05:42.980 --> 05:49.980
comic lettering, sound design, and a voice at about 190 words a minute.

05:49.980 --> 05:52.980
Leave written in code selected.

05:52.980 --> 05:55.980
Your Claude Code writes this channel's own renderer.

05:55.980 --> 06:00.980
This channel has a recurring presenter, so we said yes, design one for my channel.

06:00.980 --> 06:02.980
Click, looks right, continue.

06:06.280 --> 06:08.680
Make it yours. Give the style a name.

06:08.680 --> 06:10.680
We called it, Nobody Gets In.

06:11.580 --> 06:15.080
Next, it wants an example video you'd like to make.

06:15.080 --> 06:18.080
For ideas we took a screenshot of the channel's videos,

06:18.080 --> 06:19.880
pasted it into Claude,

06:19.880 --> 06:23.380
and asked for concepts that would appeal to the same audience.

06:23.380 --> 06:27.280
We picked 100 strangers, one bunker.

06:27.280 --> 06:29.280
Who survives 30 days?

06:30.980 --> 06:37.660
Paste it in as your example video.

06:37.660 --> 06:40.500
Open study limits and example length.

06:40.500 --> 06:47.100
We raise the study budget from 20 to 30 minutes and the most Claude requests from 40 to 80.

06:47.100 --> 06:50.980
More time gives Claude a better shot at matching the channel.

06:50.980 --> 06:55.140
Tick the box to approve the study with your Claude Code account and click study and build

06:55.140 --> 06:58.620
my style.

06:58.620 --> 07:03.060
If Studio says your study is ready to start, tick I approve continuing the saved reference

07:03.060 --> 07:07.500
study, and click continue saved study.

07:07.500 --> 07:09.540
Now Studio works through four stages.

07:09.540 --> 07:11.580
It designs around your brief.

07:11.580 --> 07:14.060
It inspects the reference frames and captions.

07:14.060 --> 07:18.260
It writes the picture style, the cast, and the voice, and then Claude writes the channel's

07:18.260 --> 07:23.620
animation and code, checking its test shots against the channel's real frames.

07:23.620 --> 07:25.140
You don't have to watch.

07:25.140 --> 07:30.140
Windows tells you when your new style is ready.

07:30.140 --> 07:35.140
Here's the finished style with Claude's test shots next to the channel's real frames

07:35.140 --> 07:36.140
and a score.

07:36.140 --> 07:39.140
Click use this style to make a video.

07:39.140 --> 07:42.140
Your example title is already filled in.

07:42.140 --> 07:44.140
Set the target duration.

07:44.140 --> 07:46.140
We picked one minute for a first test.

07:46.140 --> 07:50.140
Check the visual sources, the captions, and the creative direction.

07:50.140 --> 07:52.140
Then click create video.

07:52.140 --> 07:59.260
A quick look at the options, target duration goes from 30 seconds up to long videos.

07:59.260 --> 08:03.420
Under visual sources, sound design is on by default, and you can add stock footage or

08:03.420 --> 08:05.420
generated pictures.

08:05.420 --> 08:10.660
Under captions and publishing, you can burn captions into the video and add chapter markers.

08:10.660 --> 08:14.900
And creative direction lets you change the character or add a call to action.

08:14.900 --> 08:18.460
For a first video, the defaults are fine.

08:18.460 --> 08:20.980
Studio queues the project and works through it.

08:20.980 --> 08:26.280
It creates the narration times every word with Whisper on your computer, visualizes each

08:26.280 --> 08:29.840
scene with Claude Code, and renders the film.

08:29.840 --> 08:33.140
You can follow every step under production details.

08:33.140 --> 08:37.180
When it says ready to watch, open video, and exports.

08:37.180 --> 08:50.260
Here's the result.

08:50.260 --> 08:58.860
Day one, 6:42 PM, the bunker door seals behind you, and the lights hum on.

08:58.860 --> 09:04.460
You count heads, 100, you know none of them.

09:04.460 --> 09:09.460
The sign above the door reads, capacity, 40.

09:09.460 --> 09:14.140
You walk to the pantry, one clipboard hangs from a nail, someone has already done the

09:14.140 --> 09:28.740
math, 412 meals, 30 days. You do it again. 100 people, 3 meals each, 300 meals a day.

09:28.740 --> 09:36.980
The food lasts a day and a half. The water tank is next, 2,000 liters, 6 days if nobody

09:36.980 --> 09:45.580
washes. Then the air filter, one unit, rated for 40. At seven o'clock, a speaker on the

09:45.580 --> 09:53.160
wall clicks. A flat voice says one sentence. The hatch opens on day 30. Until then, the

09:53.160 --> 10:01.280
bunker decides who stays. Nobody speaks. A hundred people look at the same ceiling.

10:01.280 --> 10:03.920
By Day 3, there is a vote.

10:03.920 --> 10:06.880
By Day 4, there is a list.

10:06.880 --> 10:10.680
Your name is already on it.

10:10.680 --> 10:11.680
Want it better?

10:11.680 --> 10:16.120
Go to Style Library and click Improve this Style.

10:16.120 --> 10:18.960
Type one change in your own words.

10:18.960 --> 10:22.000
We wrote: too repetitive.

10:22.000 --> 10:28.600
Click Improve this Style and Claude studies the change and saves a new version.

10:28.600 --> 10:33.080
You can keep improving your style one change at a time.

10:33.080 --> 10:36.720
That's the whole thing from a brand new account to a finished video.

10:36.720 --> 10:40.320
If you get stuck anywhere, ask in the Discord, see you in the next one.

